    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d256">

                <pb facs="0471" n="371" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg371"/>

                <head>No. 255.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Morgan to Mr. Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-07-01"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 1, 1884</date>.
                        (Received July 11.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 843.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: * * * I inclose a copy of a dispatch from
                    Consul Viosca of the 17th June last, in which he informs me that Captain Caleb
                    escaped from La Paz on the 11th of May last on the Mexican steamer Estado de
                    Sonora and landed at Guaymas, whence he went by rail to San Francisco.</p>
                <p>Also a copy of Consul Kelton’s dispatch of the 7th of June, in which he states
                    that the captain of the steamer Estado de Sonora informed him that Captain Caleb
                    took passage on his steamer at La Paz under the name of John Kelly about the
                    30th of May last, and went to Guaymas, whence he proceeded to San Francisco.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>P. H. MORGAN.</signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d256-a1.xml" xpointer="d256-a1"/>
